## Why This Is Asked
This question tests your ability to handle realistic failure modes in deployed audio systems—microphone dropouts and dynamic speaker counts are common in video calls and live events. The interviewer wants to see that you can design for robustness rather than just nominal conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Online ICA with time-varying channel count and dimensionality
- Masked whitening to handle missing channels without retraining
- Cross-bin permutation alignment using angular consistency
- On-device ground-truth evaluation using play-and-record setups

## Follow-up Questions
- **How would you handle highly correlated sources?** Consider geometric constraints from the microphone array geometry, incorporate direction-of-arrival cues as prior information, or relax the independence assumption toward spatial clustering.
- **How would you trade off latency vs. separation quality?** Increase the STFT frame size for better frequency resolution, reduce overlap for lower computational load, or use a lookahead buffer with causal post-filtering to improve quality at the cost of slight additional delay.

